<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>FlociLab.Oci.Secrets</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    TWO official cloud packages, which is one more than constraint 1 allows and the fewest OCI Vault
    Secrets can be built from. Recorded as a decided exception in docs/BLAZOR-PLAN.md §14 and §3,
    with the probe and assembly evidence behind it. Real OCI splits this service across a control plane and a data plane
    that ship separately: secret CRUD is Oci.VaultService.VaultsClient in OCI.DotNetSDK.Vault, and
    reading a secret's decrypted value is Oci.SecretsService.SecretsClient in OCI.DotNetSDK.Secrets
    — GetSecretBundle exists in no other package, confirmed by inspecting both 148.1.0 assemblies.
    A sample that carried only one of them could create a secret it could not read, or read one it
    could not create.

    What this sample deliberately does NOT carry is OCI.DotNetSDK.Keymanagement. CreateSecret
    hard-requires a vaultId and a keyId (floci-oci 400s MissingParameter on either being absent,
    confirmed by curl 2026-09-02), and provisioning those would pull in a third package. Instead
    they arrive as configuration — Floci:Oci:VaultId and Floci:Oci:KeyId — which is how production
    reaches them anyway: a vault and a master encryption key are long-lived infrastructure that
    Terraform provisions once, not something an application creates at run time. The OCI Vault
    sample next door is the page that creates them.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="OCI.DotNetSDK.Vault" />
    <PackageReference Include="OCI.DotNetSDK.Secrets" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Server-side-only RCL: the shared framework already has the Components types to reference. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\..\src\FlociLab.Core\FlociLab.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\..\src\FlociLab.Oci.Endpoints\FlociLab.Oci.Endpoints.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
